  "verbalization": "Cefazolin, a broad-spectrum antibiotic, is linked to Sclerosing Cholangitis through a chain of indications that involve other antibiotics. The evidence suggests that Cefazolin may be associated with Cholangitis, which in turn is linked to Ampicillin, and Ampicillin is associated with Sclerosing Cholangitis. This implies a potential indirect relationship where Cefazolin could contribute to the development of Cholangitis, which then leads to Sclerosing Cholangitis. The presence of multiple pathways, each involving different antibiotics, highlights the complexity of the relationship and suggests that Cefazolin may play a role in the pathogenesis of this condition through an unspecified mechanism. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of considering broader antibiotic use in the context of cholangitis and its complications.",
